## The problem

Operators get hundreds of conjunction warnings a week per satellite, and most are noise. Analysts still read them one by one.

## The approach

PULSE pulls CDMs from Space-Track, scores each event, and sorts it into critical, warning or low. Behind it are four models trained on 162,634 real CDMs from 13,154 events in the ESA Kelvins dataset. I split the data by event, not by message, so the test set never leaks.

## What I'd do next

Run it alongside a real operator's workflow and measure how many analyst hours it saves.
